Tool `NASA Data:get_coronal_mass_ejection` with Parameter {'start_date': '2025-11-27', 'end_date': '2025-12-05'} on NASA Data succeeded. Result (summarized from 1664 tokens): Summary of CMEs reported (total found: 31) for 2025-11-27 to 2025-11-28

Overall patterns
- Predominant direction: NE/NNE/E; many sources at/just beyond the NE limb; one likely far-sided event.
- Instrument coverage: Frequently observed by SOHO LASCO C2/C3, STEREO A COR2, GOES CCOR-1; sources and evolution often traced in GOES SUVI 284/304.
- Notable source behavior: Prolonged filament activity spanning much of the NE quadrant (seen in SUVI 304) with gradually opening field lines and partial filament lift-offs produced several overlapping/successive CMEs on Nov 27.
- Data issues: Multiple scheduled/real-time data gaps in SOHO LASCO C2/C3; one Earth-shine event in GOES CCOR-1 affecting visibility.
- Speeds (from listed analyses): ~267–685 km/s. Types reported include Sn and Cn.

Detailed entries provided

1) ID: 2025-11-27T00:00:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T00:00Z
- Observations: First seen to NE in SOHO LASCO C2; later in LASCO C3, STEREO A COR2, GOES CCOR-1.
- Source: No clear source; likely far-sided.
- Analysis: 2025-11-27T09:22Z, 379 km/s, Type: Sn.

2) ID: 2025-11-27T02:24:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T02:24Z
- Observations: Bright, narrow CME to NE in SOHO LASCO C2/C3, GOES CCOR-1, and STEREO A COR2.
- Source: Continued outflow from on/just beyond NE limb. SUVI 284/304 show successive opening field lines and partial filament liftoff over several hours, producing several NE CMEs.
- Analysis: 2025-11-27T11:10Z, 414 km/s, Type: Sn.

3) ID: 2025-11-27T04:24:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T04:24Z
- Observations: Narrow flux rope CME to NE in SOHO LASCO C2/C3, GOES CCOR-1, and STEREO A COR2.
- Source: Continuous NE-limb outflow; subtle rising loop beyond NE limb in SUVI 284 at ~03:52Z.
- Analysis: 2025-11-27T14:57Z, 327 km/s, Type: Sn.

4) ID: 2025-11-27T08:48:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T08:48Z
- Observations: To NE in SOHO LASCO C2 and GOES CCOR-1; to NE in STEREO A COR2.
- Source: Faint rising loop from beyond NNE limb in SUVI 284 starting ~07:24Z.
- Notes: SOHO LASCO C2/C3 captured only a few frames due to a scheduled data gap.
- Analysis: 2025-11-27T22:04Z, 299 km/s, Type: Sn.

5) ID: 2025-11-27T13:53:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T13:53Z
- Observations: To NNE in STEREO A COR2 and GOES CCOR-1; overlaps with two preceding CMEs.
- Source: Likely widely opening field lines beyond the NNE limb; seen from ~12:48Z in SUVI 284; only very subtle in SUVI 304.
- Notes: Not captured in real time by SOHO LASCO C2/C3 due to a scheduled data gap.
- Analysis: 2025-11-27T18:39Z, 685 km/s, Type: Cn.

6) ID: 2025-11-27T18:45:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T18:45Z
- Observations: First seen to E in GOES CCOR-1; small portion in STEREO A COR2.
- Source candidates: (a) Filament eruption around NE limb spanning most of NE quadrant (seen erupting as early as 16:00Z in SUVI 304); (b) E-limb eruption starting ~17:16Z in SUVI 304. CCOR-1 feature may combine both.
- Analysis: 2025-11-28T01:04Z, 489 km/s, Type: Sn.

7) ID: 2025-11-27T20:23:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T20:23Z
- Observations: First seen to NE in STEREO A COR2; also to NE in GOES CCOR-1.
- Source: Most likely part of the NE-limb filament eruption spanning NE quadrant (seen erupting from ~16:00Z).
- Notes: Covered by SOHO LASCO C2/C3 real-time data gap; partially overlaps with the back of the 18:45Z CME.
- Analysis: 2025-11-28T09:41Z, 267 km/s, Type: Sn.

8) ID: 2025-11-27T23:45:00-CME-001
- Start: 2025-11-27T23:45Z
- Observations: Faint CME to E in GOES CCOR-1.
- Source: Likely eruption on/near E limb; ejecta leaving E limb in SUVI 304 starting ~22:32Z.
- Notes: Covered by real-time data gaps in STEREO A COR2 and SOHO LASCO C2/C3; CME fades before reaching CCOR-1 FOV edge.
- Analysis: 2025-11-28T07:24Z, 386 km/s, Type: Sn.

