Top winter picks (Dec–Feb) with sources and specifics

1) Joshua Tree National Park (CA) — best mild-weather desert hiking and camping
- Why now (weather): Winter days average around 60°F (15°C) with nights near freezing; humidity <25%. Source: NPS park page https://www.nps.gov/jotr/index.htm (Weather section).
- Park hours and fees: Open 24/7/365. 7-day entrance: $30 vehicle, $25 motorcycle, $15 per person on foot/bike. Source: NPS.
- Camping/hiking: Front-country and backcountry camping and extensive hiking are available (NPS Activities list confirms car, group, RV, backcountry camping; front- and backcountry hiking). Source: NPS.
- Current alerts (as of Nov 2025):
  - Queen Valley Complex closed due to flooding (Bighorn Sheep Rd, Queen Valley Rd, O’dell Rd). Updated 11/16/2025.
