- Key links: Park overview and conditions – https://www.nps.gov/jotr/index.htm

2) Death Valley National Park (CA/NV) — prime season now, but check road closures
- Why now (weather): Winter brings cool days and chilly nights with low-angled light; winter is among the most scenic times to visit. Source: NPS https://www.nps.gov/deva/index.htm (When to Visit).
- Park hours and fees: Open daily, all year. 7‑day entrance: $30 vehicle, $25 motorcycle, $15 per person. Source: NPS.
- Camping/hiking: Front‑country and backcountry camping; extensive hiking (NPS Activities). Source: NPS.
- Current alerts (as of Nov 2025):
  - Many roads closed due to flooding from storms on 11/15 and 11/18; even open roads may have standing water/debris—drive cautiously. Updated 11/19/2025. Details: NPS conditions page https://www.nps.gov/deva/planyourvisit/conditions.htm
  - Gas at Panamint Springs 7:00 a.m.–9:30 p.m. daily; 24‑hour gas at Furnace Creek and Stovepipe Wells. Updated 1/27/2025. Source: NPS Alerts.
- Key links: Park – https://www.nps.gov/deva/index.htm; Current conditions – https://www.nps.gov/deva/planyourvisit/conditions.htm

3) Pinnacles National Park (CA) — cooler temps, great day hikes, easy access
- Why now (weather): Mediterranean climate with mild winters and moderate precipitation; winters typically see highs in the 60s°F. Source: NPS https://www.nps.gov/pinn/index.htm (Weather).
- Park hours and fees: East entrance open 24/7 year‑round; West entrance 7:30 a.m.–8:00 p.m.; no through‑road between entrances. 7‑day entrance: $30 vehicle, $25 motorcycle, $15 per person. Source: NPS.
- Camping/hiking: NPS Activities include car/front‑country, group, and RV camping; front‑country and backcountry hiking; caving and rock climbing. Source: NPS.
- Key links: Park – https://www.nps.gov/pinn/index.htm; Directions (no through road) – https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/directions.htm

4) Channel Islands National Park (CA) — unique backpacking/boat‑in camping; ranger hikes most boat days
- Why now (weather): Mediterranean climate; typical highs mid‑60s°F, lows low‑50s°F; conditions vary by island and can change quickly. Source: NPS https://www.nps.gov/chis/index.htm (Weather).
- Access and fees: Islands accessible only via concessioner boats/planes or private boats; no entrance fee. Source: NPS.
- Events: Guided hikes are offered on most days concessioner boats run (leaders may vary by day/island). Ongoing, most days (long‑running regular event). Source: NPS Events (Channel Islands).
- Current alert: Santa Rosa Island—beaches/dunes of China Camp and Cluster Point, and the area between them, are temporarily closed to protect sensitive resources; travel allowed only on marked paths (updated 2/22/2024). Source: NPS Alerts.
- Example campground with numbers (Anacapa Island):
  - 7 tent‑only sites; $15 per site per night; reservations required at Recreation.gov (park ID 232502).
  - No potable water; pit toilets; picnic tables; 0.5‑mile hike from landing with 157 stairs; exposed to wind/sun/fog. Sources: NPS campground info and Recreation.gov
  - Campground reservations: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/232502
- Key links: Park – https://www.nps.gov/chis/index.htm; Weather – https://www.nps.gov/chis/planyourvisit/weather.htm; Directions/boats – https://www.nps.gov/chis/planyourvisit/directions.htm

5) Redwood National and State Parks (CA) — towering forest hikes; winter is wet but uncrowded
- Why now (weather): Coastal temps typically mid‑40s to mid‑60s°F year‑round; Oct–Apr averages 60–80 inches of rain. Dress for wet conditions. Source: NPS https://www.nps.gov/redw/index.htm (Weather).
- Fees/hours: No entrance fees listed; roads, trails, and public access open year‑round (some seasonal closures for facilities). Source: NPS.
- Events: Forest Walk: Prairie Creek (family‑friendly ranger‑led ~1‑mile walk). Most weekends Dec 6, 2025–May 3, 2026 at Prairie Creek Visitor Center (41.363822, -124.023154). Source: NPS Events (Redwood).
- Current alert: Newton B. Drury Scenic Parkway closed to vehicles Dec 1–3 for maintenance/brush removal; open to pedestrians/bicyclists. Updated 11/24/2025. Source: NPS Alerts.
