1) Anacapa Island Campground (parkCode: chis)
- Season/hours: Open year-round.
- Reservations: Required for all 7 sites; reserve via recreation.gov (https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/232502) or 877-444-6777. Fee covers up to 4 people for six sites and up to 6 people for one site.
- Fees: $15 per site per night (reservation fee).
- Sites/types: 7 total; 7 reservable; tent-only; walk/boat-to; no RVs/trailers or hookups.
- Location/access: Anacapa Island, CA 93001. From landing to campground: 0.5 mile with 157-stair climb. No roads.
- Amenities: Picnic table, food storage box, pit toilets; no water.
- Accessibility: Not accessible for wheelchairs or limited mobility.
- Regulations/warnings: Western gulls nest April–mid-August; expect guano, strong odor, noise, carcasses, and territorial birds.
- Weather: Fog any season; no trees/shade; wind/sun exposure; bring extra supplies in case boats can’t pick up. Current weather: http://channelislands.noaa.gov/news/kiosk.html
- Info/links: Camp info https://www.recreation.gov/camping/anacapa-island/r/campgroundDetails.do?contractCode=NRSO&parkId=70984; Park regs http://www.nps.gov/chis/learn/management/lawsandpolicies.htm
- Contacts: 805-658-5730; chis_information@nps.gov

2) Atwell Mill Campground (parkCode: seki)
- Season/hours: Usually late May–late Oct; potable water not always available in spring/fall.
- Reservations: Required; can be made up to 1 month in advance (https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/10044710). All sites reservation-only.
- Fees: $32 per site/night (up to 6 people); $16 with Access or Senior Pass (not for group sites).
- Sites/types: 21 total; 21 reservable; tent-only; no RVs or trailers; no hookups.
- Location/services: Mile 19.1, Mineral King Road, Sequoia NP, CA 93271; along East Fork Kaweah River. Limited services at Silver City Resort (1.7 mi E); more in Three Rivers (23 mi W; ~1.5 hrs).
- Amenities: Vault toilets (seasonal), potable water (seasonal); no showers.
- Access/roads: Unpaved, rutted, uneven campground roads; unpaved access roads OK in good weather.
- Regulations: Black bears active—use food-storage boxes; pets leashed (≤6 ft) and not allowed on park trails. More: https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/cg_regs.htm and bears info http://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/bears.htm and pets https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/pets.htm
- Weather: 6,650 ft; be prepared for three-season camping even in summer.
- Info: https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/atwell.htm
- Contacts: 559-565-3341; fax 559-565-3730; SEKI_Information@nps.gov

3) Azalea Campground (parkCode: seki)
- Season/hours: Open year-round. Winter (Nov–Apr): one loop open, 20 sites FCFS. Summer: reservation-only.
- Reservations/payment: Summer reservations up to 4 months ahead (https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/10124502). Winter FCFS is cashless via Recreation.gov mobile app QR code (download beforehand due to limited cell service; possible Wi‑Fi at Kings Canyon VC). In summer, 20 sites open for reservations in early Jan; 90 more about two weeks later.
- Fees: Standard sites $32/night (up to 6 people). Senior/Access $16/night (with valid pass). Winter FCFS fees paid via app.
- Sites/types: 110 total; 110 reservable (summer); winter 20 FCFS. RVs allowed (max 47 ft); trailers allowed (max 30 ft); no hookups.
- Amenities: Flush toilets (year-round), potable water (year-round), dump station; no showers.
- Access/roads: Paved and relatively flat.
- Accessibility: Site 30 designated accessible (level pad, firm/stable surfaces, accessible parking, extended table, raised fire ring, flat paved connection to fee station and accessible restroom).
