2025-12-01 10:28:11,956 - benchmark.runner - INFO - Here’s the up-to-date, source-backed picture for Nginx versions, docs, and what Nix/Home Manager can (and cannot) do for you.

Latest versions (stable vs. mainline), with sources
- NixOS stable channel (25.11) has nginx at 1.28.0.
  - Source: NixOS 25.11 package info: Package nginx, Version 1.28.0, Homepage http://nginx.org (from nixos-info on channel 25.11).
- Nginx mainline is available in nixpkgs as nginxMainline at 1.29.2.
  - Source: nixhub.io package history for nginxMainline shows Version 1.29.2 (last updated 2025-11-23 21:50 UTC; nixpkgs commit ee09932cedcef15aaf476f9343d1dea2cb77e261).
- Additional confirmation in the NixOS stable channel search shows both nginx 1.28.0 and (a mainline build surfaced as nginx) 1.29.2.
  - Source: NixOS search (channel 25.11): entries include “nginx (1.28.0)” and “nginx (1.29.2)”.

What Nginx branch should you use?
- The Nginx team recommends the mainline branch for most users. The NixOS module explicitly states:
  - “This defaults to the stable version. Note that the nginx team recommends to use the mainline version which [is] available in nixpkgs as nginxMainline.”
  - Source: NixOS option services.nginx.package (default: pkgs.nginxStable), description retrieved from NixOS options.

Official documentation links
- Upstream Nginx docs: https://nginx.org/en/docs/
- Upstream homepage (as referenced by the NixOS package metadata): http://nginx.org
- NixOS Nginx module options (browseable): https://search.nixos.org/options (search for “services.nginx” and specific options listed below). The exact option texts quoted below are from the NixOS stable channel.

Key NixOS module options for a quick, sane setup (stable channel 25.11)
- services.nginx.enable — boolean (default: false)
  - “Whether to enable Nginx Web Server.”
  - Source: NixOS option services.nginx.enable.
- services.nginx.virtualHosts — attrset of submodules
  - Declarative vhost config; default includes localhost = {}.
  - Example in docs shows reverse proxy to localhost:3000 with forceSSL/ACME toggles.
  - Source: NixOS option services.nginx.virtualHosts.
- services.nginx.package — package (default: pkgs.nginxStable)
  - Note about mainline recommendation as above.
  - Source: NixOS option services.nginx.package.
- Recommended presets you can flip on per vhost/module:
  - services.nginx.recommendedTlsSettings — boolean (default: false)
  - services.nginx.recommendedProxySettings — boolean (default: false)
  - services.nginx.recommendedGzipSettings — boolean (default: false)
  - services.nginx.recommendedBrotliSettings — boolean (default: false; also adds pkgs.nginxModules.brotli)
  - services.nginx.recommendedOptimisation — boolean (default: false)
  - Sources: NixOS options services.nginx.recommended{Tls,Proxy,Gzip,Brotli,Optimisation}.

Home Manager support
- There is no dedicated Home Manager module for Nginx (no programs.nginx or services.nginx in Home Manager).
  - Sources: Home Manager option search and prefix lookups returned “No Home Manager options found matching ‘nginx’” and none under programs.nginx or services.nginx.
- Practical implications:
  - On NixOS: configure Nginx system-wide via services.nginx.* (recommended).
  - On non-NixOS with Home Manager only: you can install the nginx package in home.packages, but Home Manager won’t manage the system service; you’d manage Nginx separately (e.g., via systemd/user or manual invocation).

Minimal NixOS configuration examples
- Use stable nginx (1.28.x) and a simple reverse proxy:
  - services.nginx.enable = true;
  - services.nginx.package = pkgs.nginx;  # defaults to stable (pkgs.nginxStable)
  - services.nginx.recommendedTlsSettings = true;
  - services.nginx.recommendedProxySettings = true;
  - services.nginx.virtualHosts."example.com" = {
      forceSSL = true;
      enableACME = true;
      locations."/" = { proxyPass = "http://localhost:3000"; };
    };

- Use mainline nginx (1.29.x) instead of stable:
  - services.nginx.package = pkgs.nginxMainline;

Extra, version provenance (for verification)
- NixOS stable channel (25.11) package nginx: version 1.28.0 (source: nixos-info and nixos-search).
- NixHub history:
  - nginx 1.28.0 — updated 2025-11-23 21:50 UTC; nixpkgs commit ee09932cedcef15aaf476f9343d1dea2cb77e261.
  - nginxMainline 1.29.2 — updated 2025-11-23 21:50 UTC; same commit.
  - Source: nixhub.io package versions for nginx and nginxMainline.

Bottom line
- Today on NixOS stable (25.11), nginx 1.28.0 is the stable build; nginxMainline 1.29.2 is available and is the upstream-recommended branch. Use services.nginx.* in NixOS for a clean, declarative setup; there is no Home Manager module for Nginx. For upstream docs, start at https://nginx.org/en/docs/.
