- services.nginx.additionalModules — Type: list of attrsets — Install extra third‑party nginx modules (packaged in pkgs.nginxModules).
- services.nginx.appendConfig — Type: strings (joined by “\n”) — Lines appended to generated nginx.conf; can be specified multiple times (concatenated). Use when you also use other options (unlike config).
- services.nginx.appendHttpConfig — Type: strings — Lines appended to the generated http block. Mutually exclusive with specifying the whole http block via config/httpConfig.
- services.nginx.clientMaxBodySize — Type: string — Sets global client_max_body_size.
- services.nginx.commonHttpConfig — Type: strings — Common http context defs (e.g., log_format, resolver) placed before use within server/location.
- services.nginx.config — Type: string — Verbatim nginx.conf. Mutually exclusive with other nginx.conf options except: appendConfig, httpConfig, logError. Prefer appendConfig for additional verbatim snippets.
- services.nginx.defaultHTTPListenPort — Type: uint16 — Default HTTP port if a vhost omits listen.port.
- services.nginx.defaultListen — Type: list of submodules — Default listen directives if vhosts don’t specify; takes precedence over defaultListenAddresses and other listen defaults.
  - .addr — Type: string — IP address.
  - .extraParameters — Type: list of strings — Extra listen parameters.
  - .port — Type: null|uint16 — Port number.
  - .proxyProtocol — Type: bool — Enable PROXY protocol.
  - .ssl — Type: null|bool — Enable SSL.
- services.nginx.defaultListenAddresses — Type: list of strings — Default listenAddresses if not specified (akin to defaultListen = [{ addr = "0.0.0.0"; }]).
- services.nginx.defaultMimeTypes — Type: path — Default MIME types (uses mailcap for more complete definitions than upstream).
- services.nginx.defaultSSLListenPort — Type: uint16 — Default SSL port if vhost omits listen.port.
- services.nginx.enable — Type: bool — Enable Nginx service.
- services.nginx.enableQuicBPF — Type: bool — Enable eBPF QUIC routing (supports QUIC connection migration). Linux 5.7+; elevates capabilities (CAP_SYS_ADMIN, CAP_NET_ADMIN).
- services.nginx.enableReload — Type: bool — Reload instead of restart on config changes; config exposed at /etc/nginx/nginx.conf. See systemd.services.*.restartIfChanged.
- services.nginx.eventsConfig — Type: strings — Lines inside the events block.
- services.nginx.experimentalZstdSettings — Type: bool — Enable alpha zstd module with recommended settings; adds pkgs.nginxModules.zstd to additionalModules.
- services.nginx.gitweb.enable — Type: bool — Enable gitweb via nginx.
- services.nginx.gitweb.group — Type: string — Group for CGI process (use config.services.gitolite.group if using gitolite).
- services.nginx.gitweb.location — Type: string — URL location for gitweb.
- services.nginx.gitweb.user — Type: string — User for CGI process.
- services.nginx.gitweb.virtualHost — Type: string — Virtual host for gitweb (default catch‑all).
- services.nginx.group — Type: string — Group account nginx runs under.
- services.nginx.httpConfig — Type: strings — Lines inside http block. Mutually exclusive with structured virtualHosts and recommendedXyzSettings. Use appendHttpConfig to append.
- services.nginx.logError — Type: string — Error log destination (file, “stderr”, or “syslog:…”). Level: debug, info, notice, warn, error, crit, alert, emerg; defaults to error.
- services.nginx.mapHashBucketSize — Type: null|int>0 — Bucket size for map hash tables (depends on CPU cache line). See nginx hash docs.
- services.nginx.mapHashMaxSize — Type: null|int>0 — Max size of map hash tables.
- services.nginx.package — Type: package — Nginx package (defaults to stable). Mainline recommended (nginxMainline). Supported forks: angie, openresty, tengine.
- services.nginx.preStart — Type: strings — Shell commands run before nginx starts.
- services.nginx.prependConfig — Type: strings — Lines prepended
