  - Type: Caution (potential hazard)
  - Last updated: 9/18/2025
  - Details: Leptospirosis infections are increasing in California; disease can spread to dogs and people.
  - Guidance: Keep dogs on leash in areas with beached marine mammals and carcasses.
  - Reporting: Report sick/stranded animals to The Marine Mammal Center at 415-289-7325.
  - More info: https://www.nps.gov/goga/learn/nature/wildlife-viewing-guidelines.htm

- Title: Auto-Theft Warning - Only Bring What You Need to the Park
  - Type: Caution (potential hazard)
  - Last updated: 5/23/2025
  - Details/Guidance: To prevent vehicle break-ins in parking lots and scenic overlooks: (1) remove all valuables; (2) lock your doors; (3) take cell phones and electronics with you.
