Description: For 218 years, the Presidio served as an army post for three nations. World and local events—from military campaigns to World Fairs and earthquakes—left their mark. Enjoy the history and natural beauty: explore centuries of architecture, reflect in a national cemetery, walk along a historic airfield, through forests or to beaches, and admire spectacular vistas.

Designation: (none)
State: CA

Weather: Typically cool and variable across locations. Summers are often foggy and cool; a light coat or sweater is appropriate year-round.

Directions:
- Location: North end of San Francisco at the south end of the Golden Gate Bridge.
- From north: Cross Golden Gate Bridge; take first exit from Highways 1 and 101.
- From east: Via Lombard Street (Highway 101).
- From south: Via Highway 1, exit just before the bridge.
