Scope and method
- Chain: Ethereum
- Window: past 7 days up to 2025-12-01 10:45 UTC (daily OHLCV from 2025-11-24 to 2025-11-30 plus today partial), and recent on-chain swaps (last ~10–45 minutes) for microstructure.
- Sources: DEX Paprika endpoints (networks, pools ranked by volume and transactions, per-pool details, OHLCV, recent swaps). All timestamps/amounts are UTC and on-chain.

Market backdrop (24h)
- ETH ≈ $2,840, down ~5.6% 24h (WETH/USDT references).
- WBTC ≈ $86.4k, down ~5.1% 24h (WBTC/USDT references).
- Stables (USDC/USDT/DAI) held near $1 with intraday bands typically within ±0.2%.

Top Ethereum pools by 24h volume (as of ~2025-12-01 10:45 UTC)
- MakerDAO DAI/USDC (0xf6e7…3042): $846.15M, ~2,290 tx, price ~1.0000 (tight peg)
- Uniswap V4 USDC/USDT (0x8aa4…e47): $177.66M, ~2,376 tx, price ~0.99999–1.00001
- Uniswap V3 WETH/USDT (0xc7bb…0e9b): $62.35M, ~21,178 tx, ETH ~ $2,840
- Uniswap V3 USDC/WETH (0x88e6…5640): $54.04M, ~6,533 tx, ETH ~ $2,840
- Uniswap V3 WBTC/USDT (0x5653…83b2): $37.67M, ~2,943 tx, BTC ~ $86.47k
Notables by volume: Curve USDC/crvUSD ~$19.64M; Curve USDT/crvUSD ~$17.62M. By tx count, Uniswap V4 ETH/USDT and ETH/USDC pools are also very active.

Seven-day volume leaders (sum of daily OHLCV, 2025-11-24 → 2025-11-30)
- MakerDAO DAI/USDC: ≈ $7.06B total (daily range ≈ $0.86B to $1.13B)
  • 24h price band: ~0.99914–1.00122; 7d narrow but included a brief 0.9951 low on 11/29.
- Uniswap V4 USDC/USDT: ≈ $1.04B total (daily range ≈ $0.106B to $0.220B)
  • 7d price bands: lows near 0.9948–0.9986, highs ~1.0051–1.0061; pegs solid overall.
- Uniswap V3 WETH/USDT: ≈ $313M total (daily ~$38–50M; today partial ~$30M)
  • ETH/USD 7d OHLC: peaked around $3,046 (11/26), dipped to ~$2,807 today; last ~$2,840.
- Uniswap V3 USDC/WETH: ≈ $218M total (daily ~$15–48M; today partial ~$37M)
  • ETH executions mostly $2,838–$2,842 in the recent sample.
- Uniswap V3 WBTC/USDT: ≈ $149M total (daily ~$8–33M)
  • BTC/USD eased from ~90–91k earlier in week to ~86.5k today.
- Uniswap V3 WBTC/WETH: ≈ $95M total (mix of BTC and ETH risk transfer)
- Uniswap V4 ETH/USDC: ≈ $32M total (high tx velocity despite smaller notional vs V3 majors)

What the recent transactions say (microstructure snapshots)
1) MakerDAO DAI/USDC (stables mega-pool)
- Window sampled: ~20 minutes ending 10:44:59Z; 33 swaps.
- Total traded this slice: ~6.85M DAI/USDC; largest trade 3.322M DAI → USDC.
- Prices oscillated around 1:1 with ~±10 bps; observed USD quotes ~0.99980–1.00101.
- Active addresses included aggregators: CoW Protocol (0x9008…ab41), 1inch (0x1111…a65).
Takeaway: Enormous weekly/24h flows with extremely tight peg; handles multi-million-dollar clips routinely.

2) Uniswap V4 USDC/USDT (stables)
- Window sampled: ~27 minutes; 32 swaps; total ~788k USDC.
- Largest trade: ~420,376 USDT→USDC (price ~0.999939 USDT/USDC).
- Price_0 (USDT per USDC) ~0.99992–0.99994; the inverse ~1.00006–1.00008.
- One EOA (0x66a9…ba8af) dominated activity.
Takeaway: Deep stablecoin liquidity with very small spreads; frequent arb/aggregator flow.

3) Uniswap V3 WETH/USDT (ETH price discovery)
- Window sampled: ~2 minutes; 32 swaps; ≈$480.6k notional; ≈169 WETH equivalent.
- Execution prints clustered ~$2,841–2,843 with several large prints near ~$2,813 and ~$2,795 during block bursts.
- Notable clustering in a single block (likely aggregator/MEV sequences).
Takeaway: High-frequency price discovery; momentary dislocations during bursts but quickly revert to tight bands.

4) Uniswap V3 USDC/WETH (ETH majors)
- Window sampled: ~14 minutes; 32 swaps; ~103,230 USDC for ~36.336 WETH.
- VWAP ≈ $2,840.8/WETH; intrawindow low-high ≈ $2,837.6–$2,842.3.
- Buys outnumbered sells by count and notional in the slice.
Takeaway: Consistent, tight executions around spot; sizable retail/aggregator flow.

5) Uniswap V3 WBTC/USDT (BTC majors)
- Window sampled: ~43 minutes; 33 swaps; ~2.125 WBTC (~$184k notional).
- Net: traders sold ~0.50 BTC into the pool (pool received WBTC, paid out ~43.2k USDT).
- WBTC/USD hovered ~$86.37k–$86.66k; slight drift down across the hour.
Takeaway: Moderate flow, tight pricing; directional net selling of BTC in the slice.

6) Uniswap V3 WBTC/WETH (BTC-ETH cross)
- Window sampled: ~31 minutes; 32 swaps; ~0.8425 WBTC and ~25.65 WETH traded.
- Price tight: ~30.43–30.47 WETH per BTC; implies WETH $2,836–2,845 and BTC $86.38k–$86.66k.
Takeaway: Healthy cross liquidity with balanced two-way flow.

7) Uniswap V4 ETH/USDC (ETH majors, v4 hooks)
- Window sampled: ~10 minutes; 30 swaps; ~66.91 ETH and ~178.43k USDC.
- ETH/USD price_0_usd ~ $2,839.2–$2,841.7; two raw anomalies noted but USD-priced fields consistent.
Takeaway: High transaction velocity and solid depth; very tight execution around spot.

Which pools are “standing out” this week
- For sheer volume and stability: MakerDAO DAI/USDC (~$7.06B over 7 days; $846M last 24h) is the clear leader; best-in-class for large stablecoin size with minimal slippage.
- Among stables on AMMs: Uniswap V4 USDC/USDT (~$1.04B over 7 days; ~$178M last 24h) shows consistently high throughput and tight pegs.
- For majors price discovery: Uniswap V3 WETH/USDT (~$313M 7d; ~$62M 24h) and USDC/WETH (~$218M 7d; ~$54M 24h) anchor ETH spot; WETH/USDT has the most transactions.
- BTC liquidity: Uniswap V3 WBTC/USDT (~$149M 7d; ~$37.7M 24h) leads for BTC-on-Ethereum spot.
- Notable risers worth monitoring: sUSDe/USDT pools (Fluid and Uniswap V3) showed ~$39M and ~$18.5M 24h respectively; also WBTC/cbBTC pairs across Uniswap/Fluid posted ~$24M–$23.6M 24h in the snapshot.

Token mix across leaders
- Stables dominate notional: USDC, USDT, DAI (MakerDAO/Uniswap/Curve).
- Majors secondary: WETH and WBTC pairs on Uniswap V3/V4.
- Aggregators/routers frequently observed: CoW Protocol (0x9008…), 1inch (0x1111…), Uniswap v3 router (0xe592…).

Caveats and quality notes
- Ignore outlier V2 pools with extreme “24h % change” and very low tx counts (e.g., meme/rug pairs): they can distort raw volume rankings but are not reliable liquidity venues.
- Price-change fields in some endpoints are percent values; for valuation, the USD price fields and OHLCV data are the authoritative references.
- Some Uniswap v4 pools report fee params; most listings above did not include fee but trade microstructure shows very tight realized spreads.

Actionable monitoring for the coming week
- Stablecoin routing: For large-size stable swaps, MakerDAO DAI/USDC and Uniswap V4 USDC/USDT should remain first stops given weekly volumes >$1B and <$1 per million slippage at typical sizes.
- ETH spot execution: Uniswap V3 WETH/USDT and USDC/WETH handle the bulk of ETH flow with tight bands; monitor for bursts around blocks with aggregator activity.
- BTC spot execution: Uniswap V3 WBTC/USDT remains the primary venue; WBTC/WETH is useful for cross-asset routing.
- Newer flows: Track sUSDe/USDT and WBTC/cbBTC pools; they showed strong 24h prints and may sustain higher share next week.

If you want, I can deliver:
- A CSV with daily volumes (7d) for each pool above plus rolling 24h tx counts.
- A live watchlist that flags pools when daily volume >$150M or when stablecoin pegs deviate >20 bps for >30 minutes.

Provenance and timestamps
- Data pulled from DEX Paprika: pool rankings, per-pool details, OHLCV, and recent swaps; all times UTC; latest swaps/metrics observed through 2025-12-01 ~10:45 UTC.
