- A Lyapunov-Based Small-Gain Theorem for Fixed-Time Stability (Tang, Krstic, Poveda)
  - Contribution: Small-gain theorem for fixed-time stability (FxTS) in interconnected systems.
  - Setup: Each subsystem has a fixed-time ISS Lyapunov function (FxT-ISS). A nonlinear small-gain condition ensures the full interconnection is FxTS.
  - Significance: Complements existing small-gain results for asymptotic/finite-time stability; includes analytic and numerical examples (e.g., fixed-time feedback optimization with no time-scale separation).

- ThetaEvolve: Test-time Learning on Open Problems (Wang et al.)
  - Goal: Open-source system that evolves programs to improve bounds on open problems, enabling continual learning at test time.
  - Features: Single LLM; large program database; batch sampling; lazy penalties (discourage stagnation); optional reward shaping
