Tool `Hugging Face:get-paper-info` with Parameter {'arxiv_id': '2407.10671'} on Hugging Face succeeded. Result (summarized from 183375 tokens): Title: Qwen2 Technical Report
URL: https://huggingface.co/papers/2407.10671
arXiv ID: (not provided)

Authors: An Yang, Baosong Yang, Binyuan Hui, Bo Zheng, Bowen Yu, Chang Zhou, Chengpeng Li, Chengyuan Li, Dayiheng Liu, Fei Huang, Guanting Dong, Haoran Wei, Huan Lin, Jialong Tang, Jialin Wang, Jian Yang, Jianhong Tu, Jianwei Zhang, Jianxin Ma, Jin Xu, Jingren Zhou, Jinze Bai, Jinzheng He, Junyang Lin, Kai Dang, Keming Lu, Keqin Chen, Kexin Yang, Mei Li, Mingfeng Xue, Na Ni, Pei Zhang, Peng Wang, Ru Peng, Rui Men, Ruize Gao, Runji Lin, Shijie Wang, Shuai Bai, Sinan Tan, Tianhang Zhu, Tianhao Li, Tianyu Liu, Wenbin Ge, Xiaodong Deng, Xiaohuan Zhou, Xingzhang Ren, Xinyu Zhang, Xipin Wei, Xuancheng Ren, Yang Fan, Yang Yao, Yichang Zhang, Yu Wan, Yunfei Chu, Zeyu Cui, Zhenru Zhang, Zhihao Fan.

What the report introduces
- Qwen2 series of large language and multimodal models, spanning dense and Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) variants from 0.5B to 72B parameters.
- Strong performance versus prior open-weight models (including Qwen1.5) and competitive with proprietary systems across language understanding/generation, multilingual tasks, coding, math, and reasoning.
- Multilingual capability across ~30 languages, including English, Chinese, Spanish, French, German, Arabic, Russian, Korean, Japanese, Thai, and Vietnamese.

Key results
- Qwen2-72B (base LM): MMLU 84.2, GPQA 37.9, HumanEval 64.6, GSM8K 89.5, BBH 82.4.
- Qwen2-72B-Instruct: MT-Bench 9.1, Arena-Hard 48.1, LiveCodeBench 35.7.

Availability and resources
- Open weights released on Hugging Face and ModelScope; example code and materials on GitHub.
- Resources provided for quantization, fine-tuning, and deployment to support broad application and research use.

Implementations on Hugging Face (selected)
- Qwen2.5 Instruct (text-generation, transformers):
  - Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct (Apache-2.0)
  - Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct (Apache-2.0)
  - Qwen/Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct (Other license)
  - Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct (Apache-2.0)
  - Qwen/Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct (Apache-2.0)
  - Qwen/Qwen2.5-32B-Instruct (Apache-2.0)
  - Qwen/Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct (Other license)
- Qwen2.5 Base:
  - Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B (Apache-2.0)
- Qwen2.5 Coder (code-oriented, text-generation, transformers):
  - Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct (Apache-2.0)
  - Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct (Apache-2.0)
- QwQ family:
  - Qwen/QwQ-32B-Preview (Apache-2.0)

Common tags across released models
- Pipeline: text-generation; Library: transformers.
- Tags often include qwen2, chat/conversational, endpoints_compatible, text-generation-inference, and deploy:azure. Licenses vary by model as noted above.

Summary
Qwen2 provides a versatile, open suite of dense and MoE models (0.5B–72B) that advance state-of-the-art performance among open-weight models and rival proprietary systems across a wide range of capabilities, with strong multilingual support. The flagship Qwen2-72B delivers strong base and instruction-tuned results on widely used benchmarks. Weights and tooling are openly available to enable quantization, fine-tuning, and deployment.
