Tool `Hugging Face:get-paper-info` with Parameter {'arxiv_id': '2306.01116'} on Hugging Face succeeded. Result (summarized from 335092 tokens): Title: The RefinedWeb Dataset for Falcon LLM: Outperforming Curated Corpora with Web Data, and Web Data Only

Authors: Guilherme Penedo, Quentin Malartic, Daniel Hesslow, Ruxandra Cojocaru, Alessandro Cappelli, Hamza Alobeidli, Baptiste Pannier, Ebtesam Almazrouei, Julien Launay

Core idea and findings:
- Conventional wisdom holds that LLMs need a mix of filtered web data plus curated, high-quality corpora (e.g., books, papers, social media) to achieve strong zero-shot generalization.
- This work shows that properly filtered and deduplicated web data alone can produce powerful models, significantly outperforming state-of-the-art models trained on The Pile.
- Curation at trillion-token scale is questionable; the authors show high-quality web data is still plentiful when extracted carefully from CommonCrawl.
- Scale: they derive 5 trillion tokens from CommonCrawl via aggressive filtering and deduplication.
- Releases: a public 600B-token extract (RefinedWeb dataset) and language models of 1.3B and 7.5B parameters trained on it.

Key contributions:
- Demonstrates viability and strength of web-only data for LLM pretraining, challenging the need for curated corpora.
- Provides a large-scale, high-quality web dataset pipeline and public extract to support reproducibility and further research.
- Empirically shows superior performance versus The Pile–trained baselines on zero-shot tasks.

Access:
- Paper/record: https://huggingface.co/papers/2306.01116

