Tool `Hugging Face:get-paper-info` with Parameter {'arxiv_id': '2402.00159'} on Hugging Face succeeded. Result (summarized from 30267 tokens): Title: Dolma: an Open Corpus of Three Trillion Tokens for Language Model Pretraining Research
URL: https://huggingface.co/papers/2402.00159

Authors: Luca Soldaini, Rodney Kinney, Akshita Bhagia, Dustin Schwenk, David Atkinson, Russell Authur, Ben Bogin, Khyathi Chandu, Jennifer Dumas, Yanai Elazar, Valentin Hofmann, Ananya Harsh Jha, Sachin Kumar, Li Lucy, Xinxi Lyu, Nathan Lambert, Ian Magnusson, Jacob Morrison, Niklas Muennighoff, Aakanksha Naik, Crystal Nam, Matthew E. Peters, Abhilasha Ravichander, Kyle Richardson, Zejiang Shen, Emma Strubell, Nishant Subramani, Oyvind Tafjord, Pete Walsh, Luke Zettlemoyer, Noah A. Smith, Hannaneh Hajishirzi, Iz Beltagy, Dirk Groeneveld, Jesse Dodge, Kyle Lo

What this work releases
- Dolma: a fully open, 3-trillion-token English pretraining corpus to enable transparent, reproducible language modeling research.
- Data coverage: diverse mixture of web content, scientific papers, code, public-domain books, social media, and encyclopedic materials.
- Open-source data curation toolkit: enables reproduction and further experimentation on corpus construction.

Motivation and significance
- Most high-performing LMs do not disclose pretraining data or recipes, hindering research on how data affects capabilities and limitations.
- Dolma provides an open alternative to study pretraining data composition, quality, and their effects on model behavior.

Documentation and analyses provided
- Design principles, construction details, and corpus contents are documented.
- Interleaved empirical analyses from training LMs on intermediate Dolma states examine:
  - Content/quality filters
  - Deduplication
  - Multi-source mixing strategies
- Findings are intended to guide best practices in data curation for LM pretraining.

Downstream use
- Dolma has been used to train OLMo, a state-of-the-art open language model and framework for scientific study of language modeling.

Implementations (related small models/checkpoints on Hugging Face by AllenAI, focused on data mixtures and ablations)
