Tool `Hugging Face:get-paper-info` with Parameter {'arxiv_id': '2406.17557'} on Hugging Face succeeded. Result (summarized from 174293 tokens): Title: The FineWeb Datasets: Decanting the Web for the Finest Text Data at Scale
Link: https://huggingface.co/papers/2406.17557

Authors: Guilherme Penedo; Hynek Kydlíček; Loubna Ben allal; Anton Lozhkov; Margaret Mitchell; Colin Raffel; Leandro Von Werra; Thomas Wolf

Core idea and contributions:
- Introduces FineWeb, a large-scale, high-quality web-derived pretraining dataset of 15 trillion tokens constructed from 96 Common Crawl snapshots.
- Demonstrates that LLMs pretrained on FineWeb outperform those trained on other open pretraining datasets.
- Provides detailed documentation and ablations of all curation design choices, with in-depth investigations of deduplication and filtering strategies.
- Releases FineWeb-Edu, a 1.3 trillion-token educational subset filtered from FineWeb.
- Shows that pretraining on FineWeb-Edu yields substantial gains on knowledge- and reasoning-heavy benchmarks such as MMLU and ARC.
- Publicly releases the data curation codebase and all models trained during ablation experiments.

Why it matters:
- Advances transparency and understanding of how to curate superior web-scale pretraining data.
- Offers reproducible, scalable recipes (incl. deduplication and filtering) and open resources that improve LLM performance, especially on challenging knowledge/reasoning benchmarks.

Implementations and related models referencing this work/dataset:
- BSC-LT/ALIA-40b (BSC-LT)
- BSC-LT/salamandra-7b-instruct (BSC-LT)
- BSC-LT/salamandra-7b (BSC-LT)
- BSC-LT/salamandra-2b-instruct (BSC-LT)
- BSC-LT/salamandra-2b (BSC-LT)
- nvidia/nemocurator-fineweb-nemotron-4-edu-classifier (NVIDIA)
- nvidia/nemocurator-fineweb-mixtral-edu-classifier (NVIDIA)
- axiomlaborg/Cable (Axiom Lab)
- axiomlaborg/cable-wiki-tiny-512 (Axiom Lab)
- axiomlaborg/cable-wiki-tiny-1024 (Axiom Lab)
- axiomlaborg/cable-edufineweb-md-512 (Axiom Lab)
- axiomlaborg/cable-edufineweb-md-1024 (Axiom Lab)
- fraserlove/gpt-alpha (fraserlove)
- robbiemu/salamandra-2b-instruct (robbiemu)
- RichardErkhov/BSC-LT_-_salamandra-7b-instruct-gguf (RichardErkhov)
- RichardErkhov/BSC-LT_-_salamandra-7b-gguf (RichardErkhov)
- robbiemu/salamandra-2b (robbiemu)

Notes:
- Several listed models include FineWeb-Edu in their training mixtures (e.g., BSC-LT Salamandra family, ALIA-40b) and/or reference the paper (arxiv:2406.17557 in tags).
- NVIDIA’s Nemocurator models are classifiers tailored to educational content selection aligned with FineWeb-Edu.
- Community ports include quantized GGUF variants and compact Cable models demonstrating length-extrapolation research trained/evaluated with FineWeb(-Edu).

Overall takeaway:
FineWeb sets a new open standard for web-scale pretraining corpora by pairing massive scale (15T tokens across 96 CC snapshots) with rigorous deduplication and filtering, while FineWeb-Edu targets educational content to unlock strong gains on reasoning/knowledge benchmarks. The work emphasizes reproducibility through comprehensive ablations, public code, and released models, and has already influenced a range of open models and tools.
