- google/gemma-2-27b-it (text-generation; 433,299 downloads; 555 likes; 2024-08-27)
- google/gemma-2-9b-it (text-generation; 128,878 downloads; 746 likes; 2024-08-27)
- google/gemma-2-2b-it (text-generation; 635,932 downloads; 1,230 likes; 2024-08-27)
- Base variants: google/gemma-2-9b, google/gemma-2-2b, google/gemma-2-27b
- Quantized GGUF variants referencing the paper: google/gemma-3-27b-it-qat-q4_0-gguf; google/gemma-3-12b-it-qat-q4_0-gguf; google/gemma-3-4b-it-qat-q4_0-gguf; unsloth/gemma-3-27b-it-GGUF
- Smaller Gemma 3 models: google/gemma-3-270m, google/gemma-3-270m-it
- Other: mistralai/Mistral-Small-24B-Base-2501 (Apache-2.0)

Notes on implementation tags and pipelines
- Pipelines include text-generation and image-text-to-text; many models are instruction-tuned (“-it”) and/or quantized (GGUF).
- Tags frequently include arxiv:2103.03874 along with references to core Transformer papers and licenses (e.g., Gemma license; Apache-2.0 for Mistral).

Bottom line
MATH provides a large, step-by-step–annotated benchmark for mathematical reasoning, shows current scaling limits of Transformers on rigorous math problem solving, and calls for algorithmic innovations to achieve substantial gains.
