- Roads to Butte Lake, Juniper Lake, and Warner Valley May Be Impassible (Caution — potential hazard). Snow and mud may render roads impassible. Check weather; be prepared for wet, muddy, or snowy conditions. URL: https://www.nps.gov/lavo/planyourvisit/weather.htm. Last updated: 11/19/2025.
- Lassen National Park Highway Closed for Winter (Park Closure — area inaccessible). Main park road (Hwy 89) closed at Kohm Yah-mah-nee Visitor Center (southwest entrance) and Devastated Area (northwest entrance) for the snow season. Use caution and check weather. URL: https://www.nps.gov/lavo/planyourvisit/weather.htm. Last updated: 11/17/2025.
- Visitor Phone Line Intermittent (Information — non-emergency). Main visitor phone line functions intermittently. Email: lavo_information@nps.gov for general questions. Last updated: 10/4/2024.
- Lasting Effects from 2021 Dixie Fire (Caution — potential hazard). Some facilities and areas remain closed; obey closure signs. Reopened areas may have hazards (fallen trees, loose/falling rock, undefined trails, hidden stump holes). URL: https://www.nps.gov/lavo/planyourvisit/burned-area-safety.htm. Last updated: 8/26/2024.

Joshua Tree National Park (jotr)
- Queen Valley Complex Closed (Park Closure — area inaccessible). Due to flooding. Includes Bighorn Sheep Rd, Queen Valley Rd, and O’dell Rd. Last updated: 11/16/2025.
- Oasis of Mara Trail Closed (Park Closure — area inaccessible). Closed until further notice due to heavy flooding. Last updated: 9/28/2025.
- Inaccurate Third-Party Apps (Caution — potential hazard). Some third-party hiking apps are inaccurate; use the official NPS app. URL: https://www.nps.gov/subje
