Tool `National Parks:getCampgrounds` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'yose,seki,deva,jotr,redw,chis,lavo,pinn', 'limit': 50} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 138276 tokens): Here’s a concise, information-dense summary of the provided campground entries:

1) Anacapa Island Campground (Channel Islands NP – parkCode: chis)
- Status/Access: Open year-round; primitive walk/boat-in. 0.5-mile from landing plus 157 stairs. No roads.
- Sites/Types: 7 total (tent-only); 7 reservable; group: 1.
- Fees: $15 per site per night. For six sites, fee covers up to 4 people; one site covers up to 6.
- Reservations: Required in advance via recreation.gov (campground 232502) or 877-444-6777.
- Amenities: Picnic table, food storage locker, pit toilets; trash collection. No potable water, no showers.
- Weather/Notes: No trees/shade; fog any season; wind/sun exposure; bring extra supplies in case boats cannot pick up due to sea conditions.
- Seasonal Wildlife Warning: Western gull rookery Apr–mid-Aug (guano, strong odor, constant noise, carcasses, territorial birds).
- Accessibility: Not accessible for wheelchairs or limited mobility (isolation/cliffs/boat).
- Operating hours: Open year-round (all day).
- Location: 34.0143426535, -119.367763068; Anacapa Island, CA 93001.
- Info/Regs: Laws/policies: nps.gov/chis/learn/management/lawsandpolicies.htm
- Weather info: channelislands.noaa.gov/news/kiosk.html
- Contacts: 805-658-5730; chis_information@nps.gov.

2) Atwell Mill Campground (Sequoia & Kings Canyon NPs – parkCode: seki)
- Status/Season: Usually late May–late Oct; all sites reservation-only; book up to 1 month in advance.
- Setting/Access: Along East Fork Kaweah River. Limited services at Silver City Resort (1.7 mi E); more in Three Rivers (23 mi W; ~1.5 hrs). Unpaved, rutted, uneven roads.
- Elevation/Weather: 6,650 ft; warm summers; prepare for 3-season conditions any time.
- Sites/Types: 21 total; 21 reservable; tent-only.
- Fees: $32 per site per night; $16 with Access or Senior Pass.
- Amenities: Vault toilets (seasonal), trash, potable water may not be available in spring/fall. No showers.
- Regulations: Active black bears—use metal food lockers; pets leashed in campground (≤6 ft), no pets on park trails.
- Accessibility: No ADA sites currently; commitment to create in future. No RVs/trailers allowed.
- Operating hours: Open seasonally (all day).
- Location: 36.46466811749612, -118.6696721882438; Mile 19.1 Mineral King Rd, Sequoia NP, CA 93271.
- Reservations/Info: recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/10044710; nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/atwell.htm; campground regs: nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/cg_regs.htm
- Contacts: 559-565-3341; fax 559-565-3730; SEKI_Information@nps.gov.

3) Azalea Campground (Sequoia & Kings Canyon NPs – parkCode: seki)
- Status/Season: Open year-round. Nov–Apr: only 1 loop (20 sites), first-come, first-served. May–Oct: reservation-only; reserve up to 4 months ahead (20 early-release sites, +90 more ~2 weeks later).
- Payment (winter): Cashless via Recreation.gov mobile app QR; download app before arrival (limited cell; possible Wi-Fi at Kings Canyon VC).
- Setting/Elevation: Centrally located in Grant Grove; 6,500 ft. Summer warm/sunny; winters cold/snowy; be prepared for 3-season conditions in summer.
- Sites/Types: 110 total; summer reservable; accommodates tents and RVs.
- Vehicle limits: RVs up to 47 ft; trailers up to 30 ft.
- Fees: $32 standard; $16 Senior/Access (per night, up to 6 people).
- Amenities: Flush toilets (year-round), potable water (year-round), dump station, trash, food lockers. No showers.
- Regulations: Bears—use food-storage boxes; pets leashed (≤6 ft), no pets on park trails; gates open/close at 12 pm on open/close dates; check-in 12 pm or later; check-out before 12 pm; no-show policy (by noon on day 2 site may be released); buy firewood (don’t cut trees).
- Accessibility: Paved, relatively flat roads. Site 30 is designated accessible (level pad, accessible parking, extended picnic table, raised fire ring; flat paved connection to fee station/restroom).
- Operating hours: Open year-round (all day).
- Location: 36.741334350936064, -118.96777677768745; Azalea Dr, Grant 
