Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'jotr'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 2037 tokens): - Name: Joshua Tree National Park (code: jotr)
- Designation: National Park
- State: CA
- URL: https://www.nps.gov/jotr/index.htm

- Description: Where the Mojave and Colorado Deserts meet, featuring diverse plants and animals shaped by wind and occasional rain. Known for dark night skies, rich cultural history, and surreal geology across a vast southern California wilderness.

- Location:
  - Coordinates: 33.91418525, -115.8398125
  - Address: 74485 National Park Drive, Twentynine Palms, CA 92277-3597

- Weather:
  - Generally clear, <25% humidity.
  - Spring/Fall: avg highs ~85°F (29°C), lows ~50°F (10°C).
  - Winter: days ~60°F (15°C), freezing nights; occasional snow at higher elevations.
  - Summer: hot; days >100°F (38°C), nights ~75°F (24°C)+.

- Directions:
  - From I-10, exit 117 (CA Hwy 62) for West Entrance, North Entrance, Black Rock, Indian Cove.
  - From I-10, exit 168 for South Entrance.
