- Description: Home to steaming fumaroles, wildflower meadows, clear mountain lakes, and numerous volcanoes. Jagged peaks reflect an eruptive past; hot water continues to shape the land.

Weather
- Highly variable year-round.
- Average January: high 40.4 °F (4.7 °C), low 20.8 °F (-6.2 °C).
- Average July: high 88.4 °F (31.3 °C), low 49.8 °F (9.9 °C).
- On average: 36.9 days ≥ 90 °F; 164 days ≤ 32 °F annually.

Getting There
- From I-5 (Redding): Hwy 44 east 48 mi to Hwy 89; Hwy 89 south 1 mi to north entrance.
- From I-5 (Red Bluff): Hwy 36 E 51 mi to Hwy 89; Hwy 89 north 6 mi to south entrance.
- Directions: http://www.nps.gov/lavo/planyourvisit/directions.htm

Location
- Coordinates: 40.49354575, -121.4075993
- Address: 38050 Highway 36 East, Park Headquarters, Mineral, CA 96063

