Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'pinn'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 2983 tokens): Pinnacles National Park (code: pinn)
- Designation: National Park
- State: California (CA)
- Website: https://www.nps.gov/pinn/index.htm
- Description: Volcanic eruptions ~23 million years ago created rocky spires, deep canyons, and diverse habitats ranging from chaparral and oak woodlands to cool, shaded canyon floors.

Location
- Address: 5000 East Entrance Road, Paicines, CA 95043
- Coordinates: 36.49029208, -121.1813607
- Directions: 
  - West Entrance: Via US-101 through Soledad, then CA-146.
  - East Entrance: Via CA-25 through Hollister (from the north) or via King City using Bitter Water Road (G-13) (from the south).
  - Note: No through road between the east and west entrances.
- Directions info: http://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/directions.htm

Weather
- Mediterranean climate. Summers are hot (often >100°F); winters are mild (highs in the 60s) with moderate precipitation. Expect larger day–night temperature swings year-round, and broader seasonal variability due to inland location.

Contacts
- Phone (Voice): 831-389-4486
- Fax: 831-389-4288
- Email: pinn_visitor_information@nps.gov (include visit dates/season; replies typically within one week). For volunteer opportunities: pinn_volunteer@nps.gov.

Entrance Fees (valid 1–7 days unless noted)
- Entrance – Private Vehicle: $30.00 (all occupants; East and West Entrances)
- Entrance – Motorcycle: $25.00 (rider(s); East and West Entrances)
- Entrance – Per Person: $15.00 (pedestrian or bicycle)
- Entrance – Non-commercial Groups: $15.00 per person for vehicles with capacity of 16+; capped at comparable commercial group maximums ($40 or $100). Exemptions: age 15 and under, passholders used for park entry, and drivers hired only for transportation.
- Commercial Entrance – Sedan (1–6 seats): $30.00 (price based on seating capacity; passes/ages do not alter price)
- Commercial Entrance – Van (7–15 seats): $40.00 (capacity-based)
- Commercial Entrance – Mini-bus (16–25 seats): $40.00 (capacity-based)
- Commercial Entrance – Motor Coach (26+ seats): $100.00 (capacity-based)
- Entrance – Education/Academic Groups: $0.00 with approved Educational Fee Waiver (otherwise see large/commercial group fees)

Entrance Passes
- Pinnacles Annual Pass: $55.00 (valid 12 months from purchase; covers signee and accompanying passengers in a single non-commercial vehicle; available at entrance stations)

Operating Hours
- East Side Entrance: Open 24/7 year-round, including holidays.
- West Side Entrance: Daily 7:30 AM – 8:00 PM. Access to Prewett Point, Balconies, and Juniper Canyon trails. Note: One-lane narrow, winding road; oversize vehicles should use the East Entrance.

