Tool `National Parks:getVisitorCenters` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'yose', 'limit': 50} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 3709 tokens): Summary (total: 4; limit: 50; start: 0)

All centers are in Yosemite National Park (parkCode: yose). Main contact for all:
- Phone (Voice): 209/372-0200
- Email: yose_web_manager@nps.gov

1) Big Oak Flat Information Station
- Services: Information desk, wilderness permit desk, Yosemite Conservancy Bookstore. In winter, self-registration wilderness permits for the Crane Flat area and Tioga Road trailheads only are available on the front porch. You must bring your own bear canister when the information station is closed. Wilderness permits are required for overnight stays in Yosemite’s Wilderness. Designated accessible parking spaces are available in front of the facility.
- Directions: Inside the park near the Big Oak Flat Entrance, on Big Oak Flat Road (Highway 120 from the west).
- Location: 37.8003401522, -119.875434181
- Hours: Open approximately late May through early October; daily 8:00AM–5:00PM.

2) Tuolumne Meadows Visitor Center
- Services: Information desk, Yosemite Conservancy Bookstore, exhibit area on geology, plant and animal life, and history. Accessibility: designated accessible parking space and entrance available. From the main parking lot, drive up the service road to the visitor center; park in the designated accessible space and follow the paved path in front of the visitor center to the rear entrance. Accessible restrooms are adjacent to the main parking lot.
- Directions: Along Tioga Road, approximately 50 miles from Yosemite Valley.
- Location: 37.8715673538, -119.374177997
- Hours: Open approximately late May to late September; Opening Day 2025: June 10; daily 9:00AM–5:00PM.

3) Wawona Visitor Center at Hill’s Studio
- Services: Information desk, wilderness permit desk, Yosemite Conservancy Bookstore. In winter, self-registration wilderness permits are available on the front porch. You must bring your own bear canister when the information station is closed.
- Winter relocation: Temporarily relocated in winter to 7771 Chilnualna Falls Rd; winter hours 9:00AM–12:00PM and 1:00PM–4:00PM.
- Directions: Walk from the lodge or park at the Wawona Store and Pioneer Gift Shop parking area on Wawona Road (Highway 41), then follow the marked path up the hill.
- Location: 37.5371543215042, -119.655392118492
- Hours (typical season): Late May to early October; daily 8:00AM–5:00PM.

4) Yosemite Valley Welcome Center
- Description: The NEW destination for visitor information in Yosemite Valley. Get help planning your visit and pick up free trail maps, junior ranger booklets, and more.
- Directions: Located in Yosemite Valley next to the Yosemite Village Parking and the Village Store. Shuttle access: Stops 1 & 2 (welcome center); for Yosemite Village use Stops 1, 2, 4, or 5.
- Location: 37.7465082901842, -119.58444974044362
- Hours: Open year-round; daily 9:00AM–5:00PM.
