Bridalveil Creek Campground
- Location/elevation: Along Glacier Point Road near Bridalveil Creek in red fir/lodgepole pine forest; 7,200 ft; 7 mi W of Glacier Point, 9 mi E of Wawona Road; ~45 min from Yosemite Valley. No services nearby.
- Season & reservations: Typically mid-July–early Sept; reservations required for all sites (including 3 horse and 2 group sites). Released on a rolling 14-day window at 7 am PT. High demand; most summer reservations book within seconds/minutes.
- Fees (per night): $36 non-group site; $75 group site; $50 stock (horse) site.
- Sites: Total 115; reservable listed as 116; FCFS 0. Types: 2 group, 3 horse, 41 tent-only, 0 RV-only, 0 walk/boat-to, 69 other; no electrical hookups.
- Amenities: Trash/recycling; seasonal flush toilets; no showers; cell reception; internet; laundry; amphitheater; dump station; camp store; host onsite; seasonal potable water; ice/firewood for sale; food storage lockers.
- Accessibility/RVs: No designated accessible campsites. RVs allowed to 35 ft; trailers to 24 ft; paved access roads.
- Regulations: Pets permitted (not in group sites), leashed; wood/charcoal fires permitted; max 6 people/site (group: 13–30); max 2 motor vehicles/site, park on pad (trailers don’t count if they fit); proper bear-proof food storage required.
- Links/contacts: Info: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/bvcamp.htm; Reservations: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/232453; Phone: 209/375-9535; Email: yose_web_manager@nps.gov

