General rules, operations, and weather
- Check-in/out: noon; quiet hours: 10 pm–6 am; campgrounds open 24 hours.
- Payment: First-come areas require you to occupy a site, then pay at an entrance station within 1 hour (after-hours payment allowed next morning).
- Stay limits: max 30 nights per year; only 14 of those nights allowed Oct–May.
- Site capacity (typical individual sites): up to 6 people, 3 tents, 2 cars (space permitting; some sites fit only 1 vehicle).
- Setup/food storage: all gear within 25 ft of picnic table/fire grate; store food and any scented items securely from wildlife.
- No holding or reserving sites for others; pets leashed and not left unattended; no slacklines in campgrounds.
- Weather: generally clear, low humidity. Spring/fall comfortable (~85°F high/50°F low). Winter ~60°F days with freezing nights; occasional high-elevation snow. Summer days often >100°F, nights ~75°F. Conditions change quickly; check forecasts.
- Accessibility (park-wide notes referenced below): ADA-designated campsites exist at Indian Cove (site 1), Jumbo Rocks (site 122), and Black Rock (site 61).
- Contacts: 760-367-3001; jotr_info@nps.gov

Belle Campground
- Size/type: 18 sites; first-come, first-served year-round.
- Facilities: pit (vault) toilets; picnic tables; fire pits; no potable water—bring your own.
- Fees: $25 per site; $12.50 with Senior/Access Pass.
- Access/vehicles: unpaved access roads (all vehicles OK in good weather); RVs allowed (max 35'); trailers not allowed.
- Accessibility: unpaved/uneven campsites and roads; path to bathroom is paved/flat but road to path unpaved; no ADA-designated sites.

Black Rock Campground
- Size/type: 99 sites (includes 20 horse/equestrian sites); reservations required year-round (recreation.gov or 877-444-6777). Some sites close for the summer.
