- Access/vehicles: paved access roads; RVs allowed (max 35'); trailers not allowed per site data.
- Accessibility: uneven terrain, some unpaved roads; Black Rock Nature Center ADA, paved/flat parking; wheelchair-accessible restroom. ADA campsite: site 61 (back-in), RV up to 30' (combined tow+trailer 30').

Cottonwood Campground
- Size/type: 62 sites near Cottonwood Visitor Center (southeast park). Reservations required year-round (recreation.gov or 877-444-6777).
- Seasonal note: In summer, Loop B typically closes; Loop A usually becomes first-come, first-served.
- Facilities: potable water (year-round); flush toilets; dump station; amphitheater nearby (ADA accessible from Loop A).
- Fees: Individual $35; Group $55 (3 group sites; tents only, no RVs or habitable trailers). Senior/Access: $17.50 (individual), $27.50 (group).
- Fee change: Cottonwood individual to $35 and group to $55 starting Jan 1, 2025 (noted by park).
- Weather nuance: lower elevation (~3,000 ft) and typically 5–10°F warmer than northern park; summer often >100°F; winter ~60°F days; can drop below freezing.
- Access/vehicles: paved access roads; RVs allowed (max 35'); trailers allowed (max 35').
- Accessibility: uneven terrain; Visitor Center ADA; wheelchair-accessible restroom; no ADA-designated campsites in this campground.

