Backcountry Camping in Lassen’s Wilderness
- Overview: Year-round backcountry camping with no designated sites or amenities; some areas closed to camping.
- Permit: Required for all overnight trips outside campgrounds. One permit per trip; group size max 10. Obtain online only via recreation.gov prior to arrival. Carry a copy (digital or printed).
- Fees: $6 nonrefundable admin fee per permit + $5 per person per trip (no per-night fee).
- Regulations highlights: Max stay 30 days per calendar year; some areas near developed sites, water bodies, and hydrothermal areas closed (see regs). Winter: camping allowed on/near the main park road when it’s closed. Bear-resistant containers required Apr 16–Nov 30. No pets, no bicycles, no overnight stock use. Vehicles may be left in lots for the period on your permit. Use catholes; pack out all TP/hygiene products and trash. Firearms only per valid CA CCW; hunting prohibited. Bear spray not permitted.
- Weather: Minimal precipitation Jul–Sep; up to 40 ft snow in winter; snow can linger into Jul/Aug; highly variable by elevation.
- Accessibility: No ADA facilities; OPDMDs not allowed in wilderness.
- Info/Links: Info page: nps.gov/lavo/.../wilderness-permit-information.htm; Permits: recreation.gov/permits/4675334; Regulations: nps.gov/lavo/.../backcountryregulations.htm; Contact: lavo_information@nps.gov

Butte Lake Campground (NE corner, remote; 6 mi Butte Lake Rd off Hwy 44; ~45 min from NW Entrance)
- Reservations: Required for all sites for entire season; reserve up to arrival (connectivity limited; staff/hosts do not manage reservations). 9/3–10/14: only Loop B open; water off (no drinking water or flush toilets).
- Fees: Standard campsite $22; $15 when water off. Group site $62; $35 when water off. Stock corral $37 (reservation only).
- Sites: Total 101; all reservable; 6 group sites; 1 stock corral.
- Amenities/Services: Seasonal potable water; vault toilets; dump station; camp store nearby; no showers. Generators: 8–10 am, 12–2 pm, 5–7 pm.
- Regulations: Pets leashed; drones prohibited; sites must be occupied upon payment; fees nonrefundable; stay limit 14 days/year; dishwashing at campsite only; strict firewood/fires rules; fully extinguish.
- Accessibility/Vehicle limits: Site A-6 is ADA. RVs/trailers up to 35 ft. Unpaved access road OK in good weather.
- Links/Contact: Info: nps.gov/lavo/.../butte-lake-campground.htm; Reservations: recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/234156; Phone: 530-595-6121; Email: lavo_fees@nps.gov

Juniper Lake Campground (east shore of Juniper Lake; 13-mile paved/gravel road)
- Status: Closed; work in progress to reopen.
- Reservations: Single sites are first-come, first-served; 2 group sites and 1 stock corral by reservation only.
- Fees: Campsite $12 (no water). Group site $32 (tent only, 10–15 people, up to 6 vehicles). Stock corral $30 (max 10 people, 8 animals, 4 vehicles incl. trailers; must camp at corral; no portable corrals except within enclosure).
- Sites: Total 18 single FCFS; 2 group; 1 stock corral; 3 reservable (group/corral).
- Amenities: No drinking water; vault toilets.
- Weather: Elev. 6,792 ft; typically snow-free by late June; highs ~64–80°F, lows ~25–35°F.
- Accessibility/Vehicle access: Mostly flat; accessible vault toilets; no ADA-designated sites. Unpaved access; RVs/trailers allowed (lengths not specified).
- Links/Contact: Info: nps.gov/lavo/.../juniper-lake-campground.htm; Reservations (group/corral): recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/234524; Phone: 530-595-6121; Email: lavo_fees@nps.gov

Lost Creek Group Campground (group sites only; 5 miles south of Manzanita Lake on park highway)
- Reservations: Required for all sites.
- Fees: Group site $62; capacity 10–25 people; up to 6 vehicles or one bus/RV. Each site: 3 picnic tables, 3 fire grates, 3 food lockers, parking area.
- Sites: 8 group-only sites; all reservable.
- Amenities: Seasonal potable
Tool `National Parks:getCampgrounds` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'pinn', 'limit': 50} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 2809 tokens): Pinnacles Campground (parkCode: pinn)
- Operator/Website: Operated by Pinnacles Recreation Company. Info: https://www.visitpinnacles.com/. Reservations: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/234015.
- Overview: Offers tent and group camping, tent cabins, and RV sites. Tent and group sites include picnic table and fire ring. Most RV sites have electrical hookups and share community tables and barbecue pits. Some tent cabins have electricity; each tent cabin sleeps up to 4 people. Water located throughout the campground. Oak trees provide shade at many sites. Showers and a dump station available. Pets allowed in the campground (not on trails). Swimming pool typically open mid-April through end of September, weather dependent.
- Reservations:
  - Windows: Tent and RV sites up to 6 months in advance; group sites up to 12 months.
  - How to reserve: Recreation.gov or National Recreation Reservation Service (877-444-6777).
  - Questions: Pinnacles Campground Store (831) 200-1722. Website: visitpinnacles.com.
- Regulations: Max 6 people per tent site; max 2 tents per tent site; max 2 cars per site. Follow seasonal fire restrictions.
- Weather: Park has a micro-climate; conditions can vary greatly from nearby towns. Check the park website for the most accurate forecast.
- Location: 2400 HWY 146, Paicines, CA 95043. Latitude 36.4898445959, Longitude -121.148968014.
- Operating hours: Open all day, daily (Monday–Sunday). Pets allowed in campground but not on trails.
- Fees (per night unless noted):
  - Tent Site: $43.00 (up to 6 people, 2 vehicles).
  - RV Site: $59.00 (outlets: 60A, 30A [240v], 7.5A [110v]).
  - Group Site: $110.00 (max 10 people; can be reserved 6–12 months in advance).
  - Tent Cabin Electric: $139.00.
  - Tent Cabin Nonelectric: $129.00.
- Site inventory:
  - Total sites: 134.
  - Reservable: 134.
  - First-come, first-served: 0.
  - Types: Group 21; Tent-only 83; Electrical hookups 30; RV-only 30; Horse 0; Walk/Boat-to 0; Other 0.
- Amenities:
  - Trash/Recycling collection.
  - Toilets: Flush (year-round), Composting (year-round), Portable (year-round).
  - Internet connectivity.
  - Showers: Hot year-round; coin-operated year-round.
  - Cell phone reception.
  - Laundry.
  - Amphitheater.
  - Dump station.
  - Camp store.
  - Staff/volunteer host onsite.
  - Potable water (year-round).
  - Ice for sale; firewood for sale.
  - Food storage lockers.
- Accessibility:
  - Wheelchair access: Campsites on mostly compact dirt; some loose soil; some sites not level.
  - Roads: Paved; parking spurs gravel; access roads paved—OK for all vehicles.
  - ADA info: Flush toilets and potable water provided; showers available; on-site general store with basic foods/camping supplies; swimming pool open April–September, weather permitting.
  - RVs/trailers: RVs allowed (max length 90 ft). Trailers allowed (max length 45 ft).

Key contacts:
- Reservations: 877-444-6777 (National Recreation Reservation Service); Recreation.gov listing above.
- Campground store/questions: (831) 200-1722.

